>> title: Burnt Ends
>> category: Smoked & Grilled
>> tags: beef, brisket, barbecue, smoker, low and slow
>> counters: Smokehouse
>> aka: brisket burnt ends, the point, point end, meat candy, bbq burnt ends, barbeque burnt ends
>> servings: 6
>> time: 11 hr
>> pairs-with: boston-baked-beans
>> step.2: season
>> step.3: smoke 250°F (120°C) 8 hr, to 195°F (91°C)
>> step.4: cube, toss
>> step.5: back in until the edges candy, 2 hr

Bring the #smoker{} to 250°F (120°C) over oak and hold it there.

Season @brisket point{5%lb}(2.3 kg; the fatty half, trimmed of hard fat) all over with @kosher salt{2%Tbs} and @coarse black pepper{2%Tbs}(16 mesh).

Smoke @&(~1)seasoned point{} for ~smoke{8%hr}, to 195°F (91°C), until the bark is dark and firm.

Cut @&(~1)smoked point{} into 1-in cubes and toss them in a #foil pan{} with @barbecue sauce{1%cup}(240 mL), @dark brown sugar{1/4%cup}(55 g), and @unsalted butter{4%Tbs}(55 g).

Return @&(~1)sauced cubes{} to the smoker uncovered for ~smoke{2%hr}, until the sauce has tightened onto every face and the edges have candied, and salt them with @flaky salt{1/2%tsp}.
